# Local dev: `npm run dev` serves these on the same port (e.g. http://localhost:5173/api/spotify).
# Production / GitHub Pages build: use absolute URLs to your deployed API, e.g.:
#   VITE_SPOTIFY_STATUS_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app/api/spotify
#   VITE_INSTAGRAM_AVATAR_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app/api/instagram-avatar
#
# GitHub Actions: add the same names under Repository secrets so the Pages workflow embeds them.
# If unset, the built site falls back to https://ash-chi-nine.vercel.app for both APIs.
# If both APIs live on the same host as `VITE_SPOTIFY_STATUS_URL` (…/api/spotify), the hero also infers …/api/instagram-avatar.
#
# Vercel (server-only, for api/instagram-avatar.js) when anonymous IG scrapes fail from datacenter IPs:
#   INSTAGRAM_SESSIONID=…          # sessionid cookie from a logged-in browser
#   INSTAGRAM_DS_USER_ID=…         # optional ds_user_id cookie
#
# Optional: separate API-only processes (same handlers) if you are not using Vite dev:
#   npm run spotify:local-api      → :3001
#   npm run instagram:local-api    → :3003
#
# VITE_SPOTIFY_STATUS_URL=/api/spotify
# VITE_INSTAGRAM_AVATAR_URL=/api/instagram-avatar
